<article class="env-lemma" id="0CL8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CL8">Lemma <span data-tag="0CL8">101.37.4</span>.</a> A closed immersion of algebraic stacks is a proper morphism of algebraic stacks. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      A closed immersion is by definition representable (Properties of Stacks, Definition <a href="/tag/04YL" data-tag="04YL">100.9.1</a>). Hence this follows from the discussion in Properties of Stacks, Section <a href="/tag/04XB" data-tag="04XB">100.3</a> and the corresponding result for morphisms of algebraic spaces, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04XZ" data-tag="04XZ">67.40.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>